    description: "WHAT\nScala: a parameter whose type is written infix is not typed. def map[B, C](fa: A Ior B)(f: B => C): A Ior C = fa.map(f): fa.map is unresolved. _extract_param_types_scala does not read the infix_type A Ior B as Ior.\n\nREPRO\ncats core/src/main/scala/cats/data/Ior.scala lines 906, 912, 958, 971, 973, 986 (~/whole_bunch_of_repos/cats/core). All six calls were resolved before INV-zabud only because another function of the file declared fa: Ior[A, B].\n\nFIX\nRead an infix_type's operator as the type name where the declared type of a parameter or val is read (scala.py::_declared_type_name).\n\nNOT KNOWN\nHow many calls this types outside cats."  # fc90
    fields: {}  # fc90
